00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.201
But tomorrow I'm gonna start looking.

00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:35.418
- [Mark] You start working tomorrow?

00:00:35.418 --> 00:00:37.280
- No, I'm gonna start looking.
- You start looking.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.350
It's hard right now, 'cause of the,

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.693
everything that's going on.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.320
What's going on, where are you living now?

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.620
- I'm back on the streets.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.403
- [Mark] You were staying
with a friend for a while?

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.900
- Yeah.
- But now you're back

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.743
on the streets of Hollywood?
- Yeah.

00:00:59.651 --> 00:01:01.330
I don't just stay in
Hollywood now, though.

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.560
I just, like, go wherever I want.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.133
- So you roam around?
- Yeah.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.880
- [Mark] Just stay away
from Skid Row (chuckling)?

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.520
- Yeah, I don't come down here.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.616
- Good.
- Except for this.

00:01:12.616 --> 00:01:14.010
- Except for me.
- Yeah.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:14.843
- [Mark] Cool.

00:01:17.902 --> 00:01:20.080
What's going on with the two court cases?

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:28.190
- I got court in June, early June.

00:01:32.187 --> 00:01:34.530
I'm gonna go to, it's just for

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:38.070
a plead of guilty or innocent.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:40.823
So, a plea, I guess.

00:01:44.827 --> 00:01:46.077
I'm gonna plead innocent.

00:01:47.202 --> 00:01:48.580
- [Mark] And you have
a lawyer and all that?

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.880
- A public defender.
- Public defender, okay.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:56.050
And there's two cases or one?

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.210
- I think this is just for the one.

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:01.680
'Cause the one with the--

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.330
- [Mark] The second one,
the guy's backed off, right?

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.680
- The second one, with the guy,

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.860
the one that I actually, you know.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:10.840
I think that's the one

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.693
that I'm gonna be pleading innocent to.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:17.760
I'm not sure which one it is.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.310
I think that's the one, though.

00:02:20.917 --> 00:02:21.750
- Okay.
- Yeah.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.620
- [Mark] And then what's going on with the

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.797
crystal meth and alcohol
and stuff like that?

00:02:27.797 --> 00:02:29.160
- I'm gonna be honest,

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.470
I'm super thin right now because of it.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:36.223
But I kicked it about a week ago.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.870
- The crystal meth?
- Yes.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.870
Not a week ago, maybe like
between four to seven days ago.

00:02:46.637 --> 00:02:48.693
- [Mark] Okay. And how's
that going for you?

00:02:48.693 --> 00:02:49.840
- It's going pretty good.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.250
I mean, I know I say I kick it a lot,

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:55.633
but there are actually
reasons as to why I do it.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:01.893
- [Mark] And alcohol?

00:03:01.893 --> 00:03:04.920
Is that--
- I drink every now and then.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.134
Whenever it's around or whatever.

00:03:06.134 --> 00:03:08.067
- [Mark] Do you not hit
the bottle every day?

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:08.900
- No, no.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:15.600
No, I'm not really into drinking profusely

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.860
on the streets 'cause you never know

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.610
what could happen to
yourself or your things.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:21.510
- [Mark] Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.310
What's going on with your mom?

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.843
Have you talked to her?
- Nope.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.114
- [Mark] Do you have
friends on the street?

00:03:30.114 --> 00:03:32.779
- Yeah, yeah, I know a lot of people.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:33.931
- [Mark] People you trust?

00:03:33.931 --> 00:03:35.887
- And a lot of people like me, yeah.

00:03:35.887 --> 00:03:37.370
- (chuckling) A lot of people out there.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:38.322
- Yeah.

00:03:38.322 --> 00:03:39.522
A lot of people like me.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.553
- [Mark] And your video
got a lot of views.

00:03:45.844 --> 00:03:47.803
Do people recognize you from the videos?

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.220
- No, like, on the streets?
- Yeah.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.563
- No, no.
- No?

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.000
People on the street probably
don't watch the show.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.450
- No, they don't (chuckling).

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.560
They're cool with me because I
got their back in a safe way.

00:04:10.507 --> 00:04:12.650
- [Mark] You help out some
of the people on the street?

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:17.133
- Yeah, actually, I've been
buying for the homeless.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.920
Been buying for the homeless.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.940
If somebody asks for a
cigarette, if I have it,

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.390
I give it to 'em, no questions asked.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.730
If they ask for a dollar or two,

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:31.230
I give it to 'em if I have it.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.423
Being super generous and
it's working out for me.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.120
- [Mark] That's nice, that's nice to hear.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.990
Anything bad happen to you
when you're on the street?

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.990
- Recently?
- Yeah.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.150
- On the streets, no.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:57.983
- No?
- No.

00:04:59.482 --> 00:05:01.070
- [Mark] It just seems like
there's always drama out there.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:06.070
- Yeah, yeah, but it's harmless drama.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:12.503
Actually, just the other
night, no, the other day,

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.930
I think it was yesterday,
actually, I heard this guy

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:20.330
was beating on this chick
that I've never talked to

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.970
but I've seen her around
and I went up to him.

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:27.850
And I had a metal pole and I
sat down and I talked to him

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.330
and I said, hey, did you hit her?

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.390
And he's like, only like this.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:36.300
And I'm like, I got really
angry and I yelled at him

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.610
and threatened him and I told
him, if you ever do that.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.110
And I hit his tent with the pole

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.660
and almost broke the tent pole.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.493
I think I might have.

00:05:44.493 --> 00:05:45.326
I don't know.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.160
It's probably just bent
a little or something.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:48.993
I don't know.

00:05:48.993 --> 00:05:51.730
But I told him if he ever does that again,

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:53.230
then he's gonna get fucked up.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:06:00.182
- [Mark] Quitting crystal
meth, is that something you,

00:06:00.182 --> 00:06:01.350
I mean, how has that gone?

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.523
How difficult is that?

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.090
- Me, personally, it's not that difficult

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.980
because it's not really a need to me.

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:12.350
- You're not really addicted?
- It's all in the mind.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.500
If you think you need
it, then you need it.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:16.961
- [Mark] Would you consider
yourself an addict?

00:06:16.961 --> 00:06:18.128
- No, no.
- No.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:22.610
- 'Cause a lot of people
smoke because they like

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.480
the feeling of smoke
going into their lungs,

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.280
not because of what they're smoking.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:30.733
It's not self-sabotage.

00:06:32.881 --> 00:06:34.390
It's considered calming.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.600
Smoke can help some people.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:40.566
- [Mark] Absolutely.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:44.190
People love to bash on cigarette smoke

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:46.683
but there's actually benefits to it.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:52.290
Where do you see your
life going from here?

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.440
- [Lin] Nowhere but up.

00:06:57.644 --> 00:06:59.700
- [Mark] It's nice that
you're gonna look for work.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:00.533
That's great.

00:07:04.694 --> 00:07:06.450
Are you liking California?
- Yeah.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.850
No matter how bad it gets, no matter

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.550
how good it gets, I ain't leavin'.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:14.690
Unless it's to go to another state

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:16.870
for something I need or something

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:20.097
that I feel I need to be
there for, then I ain't goin'.

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:24.520
- [Mark] Is rehab something
you think you need, now?

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:25.983
Or not so much?

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.193
You were talking about that at one point.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:31.513
- [Lin] I mean, I'm gonna be honest.

00:07:31.513 --> 00:07:35.303
If I ever feel like I need
meth because of my weight,

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.280
then I'm probably just gonna snort some.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:41.133
Because it has different
effect than smoking.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.963
- [Mark] Or just call me
and I'll buy you a pizza.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.183
- [Lin] Pizza won't.

00:07:49.496 --> 00:07:50.560
- [Mark] It won't do the trick for ya?

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:51.874
- No.
- Works for me.

00:07:51.874 --> 00:07:53.540
- [Lin] I'm just being honest.
That's just me personally.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.240
If I feel I need it,
then I'm gonna get some.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.540
I'm gonna strengthen up.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.640
It's gonna make me smarter for the moment.

00:08:01.249 --> 00:08:03.341
- [Mark] What does
crystal meth do for you?

00:08:03.341 --> 00:08:04.490
It kinda wakes you up?

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:05.890
- [Lin] It makes me smarter.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.097
It makes me really flirty.

00:08:11.097 --> 00:08:15.403
But I know my limits and I
know how to control myself.

00:08:19.941 --> 00:08:22.200
- [Mark] So your goal is to
get a job, get off the street?

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:24.033
- Yeah.

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:25.920
- [Mark] Hopefully get
past the court cases.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.780
- Well, maybe not get off the street.

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:30.343
But get a job, definitely.

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:35.623
Because I'm not even comfortable
sleeping in an apartment.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.473
I sleep on the floor whenever
I'm in somebody's apartment.

00:08:41.696 --> 00:08:42.529
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:48.066
- [Mark] What do you
think that's all about?

00:08:48.066 --> 00:08:49.080
That you're more comfortable on the street

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:52.650
or on the floor of an
apartment than a bed?

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:00.580
- Because I don't see why
people waste their time

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:03.400
and their money trying
to keep a house clean

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:10.140
and being comfortable
whenever animals don't do that

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:13.670
and they're perfectly fine.

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.100
They're natural, they're healthy,

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:17.220
they're living off the Earth.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.053
You know?

00:09:19.886 --> 00:09:20.719
Yeah.

00:09:24.599 --> 00:09:26.890
- [Mark] And you have
a brother, too, right?

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:27.790
- I have a stepbrother, yeah.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:28.623
- [Mark] A stepbrother?

00:09:28.623 --> 00:09:30.093
- A few.
- Do you ever talk to him?

00:09:30.093 --> 00:09:30.926
- No.
- No.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.460
What would you say to all of the viewers

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:41.453
that love you and relate
to you and care about you?

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.780
- I would tell them all just to be happy

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:48.373
with their lives and do
what makes them happy.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.383
And that I appreciate their
support and everything.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:57.763
Yeah.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:00.830
- [Mark] Cool.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:01.663
All right, Lin.

00:10:01.663 --> 00:10:02.496
Great seeing you again.

00:10:02.496 --> 00:10:03.760
- All right, you, too.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:06.130
- [Mark] Good luck with finding
work and everything else.

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:08.820
- All right.
- Great, thanks.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:09.653
- No problem.

